+//===- DeduBB.cpp - DeduBB tail-call basic block deduplication ------------===//
+//
+// Part of the LLVM Project, under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions.
+// See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt for license information.
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
+//
+//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
+//
+// This pass applies DeduBB tail-call deduplication directives produced by
+// Propeller (`--tail_call_profile=dedubb.txt`). The directive file marks
+// byte-identical basic blocks that end in a tail call or return:
+//
+//   bbm <id> (DeduBB.master.K)  -- block <id> is the master copy K. The
+//                                  AsmPrinter emits a global symbol
+//                                  `DeduBB.master.K` at the block start (see
+//                                  AsmPrinter::emitBasicBlockStart).
+//   bbf <id> (DeduBB.master.K)  -- block <id> is a duplicate. This pass deletes
+//                                  the block body and replaces it with a single
+//                                  jump to `DeduBB.master.K`.
+//
+// Either may end in `callees=<c>`, the targets of the block's direct calls and
+// jumps. A copy of the block reaches them from another address, so its bytes
+// differ there; a duplicate is folded only if its calls name exactly these.
+//
+// Folding is realized as a tail branch (the same instruction the
+// MachineOutliner uses for tail-called outlined functions) so that the current
+// stack frame is preserved: control jumps into the identical master block,
+// whose tail call or return then transfers control exactly as the original
+// block would have.
+//
+// Save-and-Jump (bbmsj/bbfsj) extends this to byte-identical blocks with a
+// single fall-through successor. The fold loads its successor's address into
+// the target's link register (R11 on x86-64) and jumps to the master; the
+// master ends with an indirect jump through that register:
+//
+//   fold:    leaq Succ(%rip), %r11        master:  <identical computation>
+//            jmp  DeduBB.master.sj.K               jmpq *%r11
+//
+// Nothing touches the stack and no frame layout changes, so the master's code
+// is valid in every folded function's frame.
+//
+// Two-exit Save-and-Jump (bbmsj2/bbfsj2) covers blocks that end in a
+// conditional branch. The fold passes both successors, the taken one in the
+// link register and the other in a second link register (R10 on x86-64), and
+// the master's own conditional branch picks the one to return through:
+//
+//   fold:    leaq Taken(%rip), %r11       master:  <identical computation>
+//            leaq NotTaken(%rip), %r10             j<cc> 1f
+//            jmp  DeduBB.master.sj2.K              jmpq *%r10
+//                                               1: jmpq *%r11
+//
+// Call-Return directives (bbmcr/bbfcr) are applied earlier, by the
+// DeduBBCallReturn module pass, and are ignored here.
+//
+//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
+
